- op: discuss  # d2b2
  at: '2026-10-05T11:48:23Z'  # d2b2
  by: agent  # d2b2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d2b2
  clock: 6  # d2b2
  nonce: d2b2  # d2b2
  message: "Fixed in PR #1469 (stage 9a), together with WI-losod. An atomic statement holding control flow (let x = if/match, let k = f()?;, int r = switch) runs its control flow then records the statement once, defining its variable; a nested function/lambda/closure body is its own may-run region instead of being inlined, so its bindings no longer kill the enclosing function's variables and its return no longer ends it; Java arrow-form case arms are recognised. Behavioural evidence (verify-claims fixtures, losod.md): Java switch initializer not_attempted -> ddg/confirmed; Java lambda with if, Rust let-if/let-match escaped -> ddg/confirmed; Rust let v = env::var(..)?; structural -> ddg/confirmed; closure shadowing (Go/TS/Python/Rust) not_attempted -> ddg/confirmed; sink in a Java callback unchanged. Mutation of the region bypass edge reverts them. Residual filed: WI-bufar (calling a local function variable is not a use)."  # d2b2
